The native class-action formulation now passes basic construction, JSON round-trip, and exact verification checks. At the shipping preset it has a \(11^{40}\) candidate box, a 146-bit class-group order, and a 40-entry answer; the first full public-only attack audit recovered all class-group logs as expected but the exact LLL embedding still failed after 6,815 iterations and 3,447 swaps. I’m running the full eight-seed gate suite next.
