+Paper definition.  Section 2 defines K- and O-oriented supersingular elliptic
+curves and oriented isogenies.  Theorem 7 states that the ideal class group
+acts faithfully and transitively on primitive oriented classes.  Section 5.1
+writes, for O_i = Z + ell^i O_K and class-number-one O_K, the exact quotient
+
+  Cl(O_i) ~= (O_K/ell^i O_K)^* /
+             image(O_K^*) (Z/ell^i Z)^*.
